    {
      "id": "6cec8627036a5a4e273282642d86d14a1a064a81",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3010170571,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "With this change, running Stratoshark from my build directory on Windows no longer crashes, but it prints\n\n```\n  ** (stratoshark:2092) 12:38:19.863163 [Epan WARNING] C:\\path\\to\\wireshark\\epan\\packet.c:1393 -- dissector_add_range_preference(): Unable to find dissector table for udp.port\nOOPS: dissector table \"udp.port\" doesn't exist\nProtocol being registered is \"WiMAX MAC-PHY over Ethernet\"\n ** (stratoshark:2092) 12:38:19.864251 [Epan WARNING] C:\\path\\to\\wireshark\\epan\\packet.c:1393 -- dissector_add_range_preference(): Unable to find dissector table for udp.port\nOOPS: dissector table \"udp.port\" doesn't exist\nProtocol being registered is \"WiMAX ASN Control Plane Protocol\"\nOOPS: dissector table \"ethertype\" doesn't exist\nProtocol being registered is \"WiMax Mac to Mac Packet\"\n ** (stratoshark:2092) 12:38:19.866872 [Epan WARNING] C:\\path\\to\\wireshark\\epan\\packet.c:1393 -- dissector_add_range_preference(): Unable to find dissector table for udp.port\nOOPS: dissector table \"udp.port\" doesn't exist\nProtocol being registered is \"UNISTIM Protocol\"\nOOPS: dissector table \"ethertype\" doesn't exist\nProtocol being registered is \"PROFINET Real-Time Protocol\"\n ** (stratoshark:2092) 12:38:19.868280 [Epan WARNING] C:\\path\\to\\wireshark\\epan\\packet.c:1393 -- dissector_add_range_preference(): Unable to find dissector table for udp.port\nOOPS: dissector table \"udp.port\" doesn't exist\nProtocol being registered is \"PROFINET Real-Time Protocol\"\nOOPS: dissector table \"ethertype\" doesn't exist\nProtocol being registered is \"PROFINET MRP\"\n```\n\non the console, and then shows the following in an error dialog:\n\n> Dissector bug: C:\\path\\to\\wireshark\\epan\\uuid_types.c:84: failed assertion \"(id <= num_dissector_uuid_type) && (id > 0)\"\n\nClosing the dialog closes Stratoshark. This is probably due to the fact that we put our Wireshark and Stratoshark plugins in the same build directory on Windows.",
          "author": {
            "id": 860017,
            "username": "geraldcombs",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Gerald Combs",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/860017/avatar.png?v=1788740758",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/geraldcombs"
